{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum","id":1109766,"title":"Islamic branch of the Lancea et Sanctum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T08:14:23-07:00","id":1109766,"title":"Islamic branch of the Lancea et Sanctum?","content":"B&amp;S Lancea et Sanctum seeme to very Christian-centered, do Muslim (and Jewish) Sanctified exist in 2ed?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because they are somewhat necessary for a game setting I'm writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:20:06-07:00","id":1109772,"title":"","content":"There were branches in first edition. They might be separate covenants in second, with the same religious bent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:27:58-07:00","id":1109776,"title":"","content":"Given the mythic origin of the Lancea et Sanctum is pretty inextricably tied to early Christianity, it's not likely... but not impossible for Sanctified to adapt their philosophy to similar-yet-different monotheistic faiths. Probably named themselves something different, but the practices involved are recognizably similar?<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are others here who are more well-read as far as supplements go, and can correct my assumptions if any published material contradicts them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:35:58-07:00","id":1109796,"title":"","content":"There was a passing reference to the Iblic Creed in Secrets of the Covenants, but that that's about it. As others have noted, Lancea et Sanctum is not just Christian, it is a specifically Catholic organisation. Your best be if you want to include the Banu Shaitan is to make them a related, but separate covenant with their own philosophy, theology and hierarchy. I'd suggest that you start with Islamic perspectives on Isa (Jesus), and the Islamic version of Crucifixion, then work you way out from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T14:12:25-07:00","id":1109928,"title":"","content":"Or adapt the Ashirra from the Veil of Night supplement for Dark Ages. (The Ashirra could be described as if the Invictus took Islam as its central governing element).<br /> <br /> Another idea that was suggested was making an Islamic covenant somewhat Carthian in nature: the leading imams, qadis, and other authorities pass judgments about how to integrate vampiric and Islamic life, which become enforced through a process similar to Carthian Law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T14:32:02-07:00","id":1109932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1109928#post1109928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or adapt the Ashirra from the Veil of Night supplement for Dark Ages. (The Ashirra could be described as if the Invictus took Islam as its central governing element).<br /> <br /> Another idea that was suggested was making an Islamic covenant somewhat Carthian in nature: the leading imams, qadis, and other authorities pass judgments about how to integrate vampiric and Islamic life, which become enforced through a process similar to Carthian Law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the legalistic bent of most Islamic denominations, that is an excellent idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T14:59:00-07:00","id":1109938,"title":"","content":"Yes, they exist. Everything from 1e still exists in 2e. There's not a lot of <i>support</i> for it, but it exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-30-2017, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T18:12:31-07:00","id":1109983,"title":"","content":"The Lancea et Sanctum is not Christian at all. I really don't understand why that is so difficult to understand and accept. Jesus is not the central figure of LS. It would be Longinus. The Sanctified are Longinian, no Christians, Muslims, or Jews to be found. The oldest and largest Creed has a facade of Catholicism and is associated with the Catholic church. Other Creeds are associated with other Christian churches. There is a Creed associated with Muslims and another with Jews.<br /> <br /> I would assume the Muslim view of Longinus is that he was a Jinn. I imagine the Creed associated with Islam focuses strongly on the role of tempter and protector of Muslims. I'm not so clear on the Jewish Creed. When they are both present I would go with them being more academic to contrast the two Creeds. Each would have an appearance of an associated religion like the standard option of LS has the Catholic appearance. However, with different focuses they would be a bit more distinction than LS with Muslim skin and LS with Jewish skin.<br /> <br /> In that way, it would be like having two local covenants that share Theban and LS merits, but with their own unique identity. The actual Muslim and Jewish vampires would likely be Invictus or Carthian. Becoming Sanctified means giving up mortal religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T01:14:40-07:00","id":1110093,"title":"","content":"Diggs is right, Longinus is the first and to date only prophet God sent to Kindred as opposed to Mohamed who was the last to be sent to mankind so it should be pretty easy to tie those two concepts together but The Lancea et Sanctum is it's own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T08:28:30-07:00","id":1110176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1109928#post1109928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea that was suggested was making an Islamic covenant somewhat Carthian in nature: the leading imams, qadis, and other authorities pass judgments about how to integrate vampiric and Islamic life, which become enforced through a process similar to Carthian Law.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's amazing, this is definitely the idea I'll be building on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:18:49-07:00","id":1110245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1109983#post1109983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea et Sanctum is not Christian at all. I really don't understand why that is so difficult to understand and accept.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because its easy to mistake the trappings and exaggerate the rest. Especially when the covenant's holy book and history reflect the life of Jesus, and outright mimics the Bible. The comparisons are very heavy to the point of being hard to ignore.<br /> <br /> On another note, there is a bit of description of the Islamic version in Ancient Mysteries book. I forget the name and stuff, but its there. Yes, the islamic covenant used Theban, and they had a focus on academics as well, though we never got to see any islamic themed rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-01-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:22:23-07:00","id":1110249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110245#post1110245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because its easy to mistake the trappings and exaggerate the rest. Especially when the covenant's holy book and history reflect the life of Jesus, and outright mimics the Bible. The comparisons are very heavy to the point of being hard to ignore.<br /> <br /> On another note, there is a bit of description of the Islamic version in Ancient Mysteries book. I forget the name and stuff, but its there. Yes, the islamic covenant used Theban, and they had a focus on academics as well, though we never got to see any islamic themed rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are called the Banu Shitian, and they uphold the Iblic Creed I meantioned above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:31:26-07:00","id":1110255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110245#post1110245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because its easy to mistake the trappings and exaggerate the rest. Especially when the covenant's holy book and history reflect the life of Jesus, and outright mimics the Bible. The comparisons are very heavy to the point of being hard to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Testament of Longinus reflects the life of Longinus, not Jesus. Diggs is right, people are overexaggerating the necessity for Jesus or Christian or Catholic-oriented beliefs in the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> They're cursed by god. That's the point. Whether its for killing Jesus, for refusing to bow down to Adam, or however else these religions have demonized the other, they're cursed by god. That's the core of the Lancea et Sanctum. They're cursed, but not entirely useless and maybe one day they'll find redemption in doing gods will, even if it isn't the same as offered to humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:12:18-07:00","id":1110267,"title":"","content":"I'm one of those people who prefers the Lancea et Sanctum as purely Christian. A big part of Longinus' backstory is him being spontaneously Embraced by the blood of Jesus- seeing as how many Jews don't hold that Jesus was a prophet, and that Muslims reject the idea of Jesus being divine for metaphysical reasons, that's kind of a sticking point. It may seem silly to a lot of us today, but I think such differences that were grounds for religious conflict between Christians, Jews, and Muslims in life would still be pretty much insurmountable in death.<br /> <br /> I prefer the idea that Jewish and Muslim Kindred have their own vampiric faiths. That said, I can see Muslim Kindred being closer in outlook and objectives to Sanctified, perhaps following what they believe to be a lost Sura that gives instructions for the conduct of vampires, protecting faithful Muslims and punishing apostates, pushing non-Muslims closer towards converting, etc. I think Theban Sorcery makes sense for them: we already know Theban Sorcery predates the Sanctified, so why do they get exclusive rights to it? That said, I'm also cool with them getting modified Carthian Law thanks to Islam's strong legal component. <br /> <br /> The Jewish equivalent... that's a bit harder for me to pin down. I think their obvious divergence point would be thinking that Kindred are children of Lilith. Perhaps some sort of reflection of the idea that Israel is the chosen people of God? The Bar Lilith being Lilith's favorite children? Again, I can hear an argument for them getting Theban Sorcery, but association with a female genitrix screams Cr\u00faac. At the same time, Judaism's heavy focus on oaths and covenants suggests something mirroring Invictus Oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T11:23:09-07:00","id":1110274,"title":"","content":"There is mentioning of Islamic Covenant, similar to Lancea et Sanctum in <i>Soulless &amp; Dead</i> Dark Era from <b>Dark Eras Companion</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DEC, p. 91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Al-Hamasoun</b><br /> As Christianity is not the only religion in Europe, so too are the Lancea et Sanctum not the only religious among the Kindred. While most Jewish vampires keep their religious unlives (if any) separate from their Requiems, many Muslims among the Kindred have sought a mystical path framework. The Al-Hamasoun consider themselves to be fulfilling the role of Iblis, a Jinni so proud that he would not prostrate himself before Adam, even though God commanded it. Iblis himself was made of fire, he said, and Adam was made of earth. Why should he obey him?<br /> <br /> In response, the Al-Hamasoun say, God cursed Iblis, consigning him to a prison of inanimate flesh and making him vulnerable to fire. Iblis, however, still believed that he was right, and made it his mission to prove to God the debased and unworthy nature of man. The Al-Hamasoun, therefore, see it as their spiritual duty to corrupt, degrade, and tempt man into turning away from God and toward sin.<br /> <br /> Despite their similarities, the Al-Hamasoun conflict frequently with the Lancea et Sanctum, though both sides are frequently more motivated by selfish power jockeying and greed, and later justified with religious rhetoric, than the reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-01-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T13:52:21-07:00","id":1110341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1109983#post1109983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea et Sanctum is not Christian at all. I really don't understand why that is so difficult to understand and accept. Jesus is not the central figure of LS. It would be Longinus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the significance of Longinus is entirely predicated on the divinity of Jesus - that is how he became a vampire, and how he realised God had a purpose for vampires. His whole legend is explicitly Christian, and built on events that only have significance in a Christian context (Jesus means nothing in Judaism, while in Islam another was crucified in his place).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110255#post1110255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Testament of Longinus reflects the life of Longinus, not Jesus. Diggs is right, people are overexaggerating the necessity for Jesus or Christian or Catholic-oriented beliefs in the Lancea et Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that life is the life of the Roman Centurion who stuck a spear into Jesus's side and proclaimed his divinity. If you want a vampiric religion that works equally as a current beneath Christian. Islamic, and Judaic surfaces, then don't pick a central figure that is a Christian legend and whose significance only makes sense in a Christian context. If you do pick such a figure, then admit the fact that the religion you've created has far more to do with Christianity than with Islam or Judaism.<br /> <br /> [I do realise <i>you</i> didn't create the Lancea - it's just a rhetorical device]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:14:21-07:00","id":1110351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110341#post1110341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the significance of Longinus is entirely predicated on the divinity of Jesus - that is how he became a vampire, and how he realised God had a purpose for vampires. His whole legend is explicitly Christian, and built on events that only have significance in a Christian context (Jesus means nothing in Judaism, while in Islam another was crucified in his place).]</div> </div> </div> </div>This. A Muslim vampire isn't going to start believing that Jesus was divine just because he got Embraced, and a Christian vampire, even if her new faith is a mockery of her old, is going to take somebody saying that the central figure of her old faith who is now a key but tangential figure of her new faith wasn't actually involved in THE key event of both faiths. She's going to look at him and say, &quot;Well if Jesus didn't get crucified, how the hell did Longinus get Embraced, genius?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Like it or not, the flavor of the Lancea et Sanctum is now firmly Christian thanks to the 2e corebook and SotC- though as Dark Eras confirms, not purely Catholic/Orthodox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:45:12-07:00","id":1110372,"title":"","content":"It is incredibly easy to create the Muslim Creed of the Sanctified. Look to Muslim organization and ritual as a basis for the same in the Sanctified. Longinus exists as the prophet for Kindred. Kindred are not human. Adjust the minor detail of the Longinus story to match everything up with that. I'm sure Sanctified of the Christian Creeds would pitch a fit, but they could get along in the same covenant.<br /> <br /> For Jews, I would look to Kabbalah, but I have no idea how the Testament would need to be altered. I don't know enough about it.<br /> <br /> I don't think in the same domain Christian, Muslim, and Jewish Creeds have a place. Maybe Muslim and Jewish would work in the same place. Jews have a legal system too so they could easily have modified Law. Either Law or Oaths. It might be fitting to tie the less devout to the Carthians and Invictus with the Muslim and Jewish covenant/creeds picking one or the other with which to ally.<br /> <br /> Any way you look at it, Kindred will not be devout Muslim or Jew, and the same goes for Christians. Kindred that were devout as mortals could easily transfer their faith to the Lancea et Sanctum or equivalent. I think it is important to consider that. To those that actually understand the Lancea et Sanctum, it functions as a place for devout Christians to go when they become Kindred and lose their faith in Christianity. Muslims and Jews would need to have their place to do that and a covenant would need to reflect that conversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:49:31-07:00","id":1110377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110351#post1110351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Well if Jesus didn't get crucified, how the hell did Longinus get Embraced, genius?!&quot;<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Allah willed it. And Longinus is Allah's prophet to Kindred. Longinus predates Allah's last prophet so there is no conflict at all, actually. Having said that, I would expect Muslims to be as welcoming to that as the Catholic church is to the Lancea et Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T15:01:32-07:00","id":1110382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110341#post1110341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that life is the life of the Roman Centurion who stuck a spear into Jesus's side and proclaimed his divinity. If you want a vampiric religion that works equally as a current beneath Christian. Islamic, and Judaic surfaces, then don't pick a central figure that is a Christian legend and whose significance only makes sense in a Christian context. If you do pick such a figure, then admit the fact that the religion you've created has far more to do with Christianity than with Islam or Judaism.<br /> <br /> [I do realise <i>you</i> didn't create the Lancea - it's just a rhetorical device]</div> </div> </div> </div>When people ask for an Islamic branch or version of the Lancea et Sanctum, they are not talking about a Longinus-based covenant. It's not 'Longinus went to the Middle East and formed a Mosque and prayer group.' It's just as easily 'someone refused to bow down before Adam when Allah demanded it, and so they are banished from his light and love forever,' becoming a vampire. See? No Longinus, but you have the basis for a similar group. For all that people keep bringing up Jesus or Longinus, they matter very little to what the covenant does. This shouldn't be so hard to understand, especially since we have examples of it across the other covenants. The Invictus may organize themselves as a neo-feudal realm in one domain, with a Prince and Dukes and lesser 'noble' terms beneath them. But in another domain they may organize themselves as a corporation, with a CEO and a board of elders. Just like the Circle of the Crone may organize themselves around some Grecian Pantheism in one domain, and straight up Anton LaVey Beast-worship in another.<br /> <br /> Jesus and Longinus aren't what the Lancea et Sanctum are really about. That's just fluff, like one vampire dressing as a reverend and one portraying themselves as a robed monk. That's how they go about their belief in a higher force, its judgment of them, and their reaction to it. Changing that god to Allah or Yeshua or even some abstract form of Nirvana is not a roadblock. In the end you have the same thing, an organized religion, people who believe their undeath is a direct result of the powers within it, and them bringing it into their Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T15:04:27-07:00","id":1110385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110377#post1110377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allah willed it. And Longinus is Allah's prophet to Kindred. Longinus predates Allah's last prophet so there is no conflict at all, actually. Having said that, I would expect Muslims to be as welcoming to that as the Catholic church is to the Lancea et Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I supposed it could be something akin to the split between Catholics/Eastern Orthodox and Miaphysite (aka Oriental Orthodox) Christians- yes, they both follow the same guy, but the specifics lead to some pretty serious disagreements. And yeah, I fully expect Sanctified from Christian backgrounds to have limited-at-best patience for Sanctified from Muslim backgrounds- and vice-versa. I don't exactly see those creeds cohabiting in the same domain peacefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T16:06:23-07:00","id":1110397,"title":"","content":"you know, even if you call the Lancea a Longian religion, Longinus is still a Christian character. Him stabbing Jesus with the spear is an iconic, Christian image. The reason people call the Lancea &quot;christian&quot; is because their ideology heavily relays on Christian symbolism. Sure, you could say that Longinus is &quot;just the fluff&quot;- but heck, the fluff is important. In the same way you could say that the Circle of the Crone don't really need to be pagans, as all of the paganism is just an aesthetic and not what the Circle is really about. While the Lancea are not Christian, they have originated from Christianity, and it still influence the way they structure themselves. Beside, I would also like to remind that we do have an Orthodox parallel to the Lancea at 2E, as detailed in Athens's setting. Covenants are much more localized in the new edition, so it would make more sense for a separate Muslim and Jewish covenants to exist, than them being simply Creeds of the Lancea.<br /> <br /> Now, we should also remember that a lot of it would depend on the amount of power the Lancea have in the region- if they are the top dogs of the city, be sure that they won't let to any competitors to exist in their turf. They'll probably have Creeds with modified religion, meant to include vampires of other religions who seek for a way to practice their faith even after death, even if in a perverted way. But we should also remember that the covenants are made from the vampires who make it, and that they had their own religion and faith before the Embrace. It doesn't make sense for a setting with a strong Muslim or Jewish (heck, even Orthodox) presence to simply embrace the teaching of Longinus and the Lancea. Jewish and Muslim vampires have probably developed their own heresies, built around their own ideas and belief system which are as different from their original religion as the Lancea are from Christianity.<br /> <br /> In sort, yes, the Lancea have Christian roots, and yes, those roots matter, and yes, the Lancea are not Christian. Yes, it may have certain factions which try to convert as many undead souls as possible to their Church by bending their faith so it could be more well received among others, and yes, there could still be other covenants which parallel other religions. All answers are correct- and a lot of it depends on the setting. There is no reason why the Lancea couldn't have its own &quot;muslim creed&quot; in order to convert more vampires, but saying that it should take the place of every Abrahamic covenants around the world is ridiculous, especially since it is not meant to be a &quot;catchall&quot; Covenant for every vampire who follows the Abrahamic religion in the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T16:26:36-07:00","id":1110401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110382#post1110382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people ask for an Islamic branch or version of the Lancea et Sanctum, they are not talking about a Longinus-based covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what's with all the Longinus-not-Jesus-so-it's-not-Christian argument? Which you yourself posted in support of?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This shouldn't be so hard to understand, especially since we have examples of it across the other covenants. </div> </div> </div>It's not hard to &quot;understand,&quot; thankyou very much. It's a disagreement that you can swap out all the names, myths, history, social structure - all the things covenants like this use to define themselves - and say it's a brach of the same group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Invictus may organize themselves as a neo-feudal realm in one domain, with a Prince and Dukes and lesser 'noble' terms beneath them. But in another domain they may organize themselves as a corporation, with a CEO and a board of elders. </div> </div> </div>The Invictus are different. Their ethos is &quot;whatever works for power&quot; and they'll use and recognise whatever form of power works in a given area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like the Circle of the Crone may organize themselves around some Grecian Pantheism in one domain, and straight up Anton LaVey Beast-worship in another. </div> </div> </div>Which is why the Circle of the Crone was described in its sourcebook as a catch-all for many different covenants rather than one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jesus and Longinus aren't what the Lancea et Sanctum are really about. That's just fluff, like one vampire dressing as a reverend and one portraying themselves as a robed monk. That's how they go about their belief in a higher force, its judgment of them, and their reaction to it. Changing that god to Allah or Yeshua or even some abstract form of Nirvana is not a roadblock. </div> </div> </div>It <i>should</i> be a roadblock if the covenant is to anything but bland pap, because no one who believes in God thinks God is &quot;just fluff&quot; - and no covenant made up of such believers will be organised in a way that treats God as fluff. I don't see how <i>that</i> is hard to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T17:39:51-07:00","id":1110418,"title":"","content":"Wow I just wanted advice for a game and this turned into a full-blown argument, good job guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T18:13:40-07:00","id":1110425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110401#post1110401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what's with all the Longinus-not-Jesus-so-it's-not-Christian argument? Which you yourself posted in support of?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I explained further in my post, the trappings are easily changeable. Me explaining that the Testament of Longinus is about Longinus and not Jesus is just correcting MCN.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not hard to &quot;understand,&quot; thankyou very much. It's a disagreement that you can swap out all the names, myths, history, social structure - all the things covenants like this use to define themselves - and say it's a brach of the same group. </div> </div> </div>So call it a variant. There is trouble understanding, you can be glib about it if you want but the mere fact we're having this discussion over and over should be a obvious proof of it. You're placing an emphasis on one side of the Lancea et Sanctum, the trappings of Christianity, and not what the core of the group is, an organized religion, vampirism a curse from a higher being and 'a bad thing.' If it makes you feel better, you can blame me, and say I'm placing an emphasis on one side of the Lancea et Sanctum, and not paying attention to what you deem important, but the difficulty in discussing this is based on that, regardless of where we place blame. I've explained the difference right here. Some people are placing an emphasis on the trappings, some on the core message. And it's been frequently brought up not just in this thread, but the other threads we've made about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Invictus are different. Their ethos is &quot;whatever works for power&quot; and they'll use and recognise whatever form of power works in a given area. </div> </div> </div>They're conservative traditions and order. It brings the Beast to heel. It's why an Oath can leash the Beast, which Humanity cannot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why the Circle of the Crone was described in its sourcebook as a catch-all for many different covenants rather than one. </div> </div> </div>Yes. And why the Lancea et Sanctum in its sourcebook has both a Jewish and a Muslim variant that do not revere Longinus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It <i>should</i> be a roadblock if the covenant is to anything but bland pap, because no one who believes in God thinks God is &quot;just fluff&quot; - and no covenant made up of such believers will be organised in a way that treats God as fluff. I don't see how <i>that</i> is hard to understand. </div> </div> </div>Because the characters who make up the covenant aren't part of the writers or homebrewers making it in the first place? Just like it's not 'Longinus opening up a Mosque,' it is not 'Longinus going to the Middle East and setting up a LS franchise, telling people 'hey it's the same god just do what I do.'' This is a conscious decision from creators who want a similar in-game goal, like I said before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T18:22:55-07:00","id":1110428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110418#post1110418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow I just wanted advice for a game and this turned into a full-blown argument, good job guys</div> </div> </div> </div>Not your fault. It always ends up this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":".  claims to the contrary and not about to start a new argument 07-01-2017, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T19:06:56-07:00","id":1110439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110428#post1110428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not your fault. It always ends up this way because there are people on these forums that hate Christianity and get their jollies bashing the Lancea Sanctum in place of Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps we have a background in religious studies, recognize telltale signs of Christian Apocrapha in the LeS, particularly I the Testment of Longinus, and have have experience with the Islamic (or Jewish) faith, so we see why they wouldn't buy into a Christian derived vampiric faith. Diggs, you have some awesome and cool of how to make the Banu Shaitan work within a Lancea framework, but it is incredibly unfair to suggest that those with other perspectives are disagreeing with you because we have an ax to grind. Especially when the reason we are so passionate is because we have degrees in that area, or because we have family ties to multiple faiths. Or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T19:13:18-07:00","id":1110441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110418#post1110418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow I just wanted advice for a game and this turned into a full-blown argument, good job guys</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. My advice is the Carthian Law-esque version. And for it to be less arguably Islamic than the Lancea is Chrsitian - if that makes sense - because Islam already has the concept of nonhuman adherents in its mythology, and it would be a shame not to take advantage of that bit of atmosphere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":".  Removing a response to a deleted comment 07-02-2017, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T20:23:02-07:00","id":1110453,"title":"","content":"I'm aware of Jewish and Islamic courts but I have no experience with them.<br /> <br /> Why doesn't someone offer a solution to Carthian Law as a Muslim thing? Would there not need to be restriction on who makes up the body of law? Would the Law work on those outside the covenant? Would it be more based on territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T21:52:45-07:00","id":1110466,"title":"","content":"I think that if one were to expand the Iblic Creed, they'd need to take the emphasis off of Longinus' role in the crucifixion, considering Isa didn't even die on the cross in most Islamic versions of the event. No, the emphasis should instead be placed on his meeting with Amoniel; that's when he became a Prophet.<br /> The Iblic Creed might hold very different accounts of Longinus' life and Requiem, but his message remains the same; that Vampire's are God's holy monsters, damned but offered divine purpose.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine the end result would probably appear almost as different to the mainstream Lancea Et Sanctum as Islam does from Christianity, but the central practices of the two are probably somewhat closer. Perhaps the most visible difference would be the lack of spear symbolism, which is probably why they don't use the same name for the Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T04:41:41-07:00","id":1110511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Testament of Longinus reflects the life of Longinus, not Jesus.</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem is that Longinus' life itself reflects a vampire version of Jesus. The similarities between the two are incredably heavy. Longinus has his start as at Golgatha as well. And that's just the history - the overwhelming majority of mechanics, modern night descriptions, roles in the covenant, and other trappings are heavily Christian themed. <br /> <br /> While Longinus may not be Jesus, that difference is literally only academic. Realistically? In common language of the ley person? The difference is so slight its ultimately meaningless in the long run. That's the fun thing about social language - its figurative, not literal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Like it or not, the flavor of the Lancea et Sanctum is now firmly Christian thanks to the 2e corebook and SotC- though as Dark Eras confirms, not purely Catholic/Orthodox.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> This. 2e firmly places the Lance as so heavily Christian-themed to make the other religions all but impossible as part of it. I'd love to see some jewish or islamic rites, but I don't think that's going to happen anytime soon.</span> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've said it elsewhere, and I'll say it here again. If you want to make Islam a covenant, starting with some of the mechanics of the Lancea et Sanctum is a good place. The focus on academia and Theban Sorcery -do- fit into the religion. You'll need to change things around a bit, and quite likely device some new rituals, but there are a number of things that do fit very well into Islam. While I'm not going to say that they should be the same covenant, I do think that you could take the Lance's covenant advantages into something Islamic-based most easily than any other, and its far easier than going from scratch. Now, I don't know enough of Islam to say what would make good miracles, or if taking shelter in a masque works like it does in a church or temple, but its definitely a good starting point. These two religions do share enough in common that its easier, from a design stand point, to move mechanics over and rewrite the fluff than to remake everything from scratch.<br /> <br /> And, yes, that history and holy book and other social influences do matter. After all, we're talking about a covenant, and these are, above all else, social constructs in a Social-political game. These trappings matter more than the actual mechanics. <br /> <br /> That said, you also do need to keep in mind that these are -vampires- and not actual Muslims if you do go with this. Too often I see people do a direct transplant of &quot;vampries who religiously follow the Quran with no consideration of vampire-nature&quot; when this subject comes up. Covenants are -not- for human mindsets. They're for vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:43:09-07:00","id":1110542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110511#post1110511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it elsewhere, and I'll say it here again. If you want to make Islam a covenant, starting with some of the mechanics of the Lancea et Sanctum is a good place. The focus on academia and Theban Sorcery -do- fit into the religion. ... That said, you also do need to keep in mind that these are -vampires- and not actual Muslims if you do go with this. Too often I see people do a direct transplant of &quot;vampries who religiously follow the Quran with no consideration of vampire-nature&quot; when this subject comes up. Covenants are -not- for human mindsets. They're for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier, Islamic mythology includes the potential for nonhuman adherents in a way that Christian mythology doesn't, so that's a good bit of atmosphere to include. Which is why I often recommend Veil of Night's Ashirra as a model. They are built around attempts to adapt Islam to vampiric natures and concerns.<br /> <br /> That said, it doesn't have to be just one covenant.<br /> <br /> If an Islamic-world covenant has an analogue for the Lancea's creed, they might take after the myth of the qarin - special djinn who are doubles of each person and tempt them to evil. They obviously can't <i>be</i> that, but they could believe that each person having a qareen is a metaphor for vampires being qarin of humanity in general. Their job is to tempt and test humanity, but also to accept good guidance from humanity. Rather than being damned, I think it would make more sense if they believed they were always qarin and their embrace was a foreordained fate to mark the beginning of their appointed task - their seemingly human life being to teach them the good and bad about humanity.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a more social and legalist covenant could try to reconcile Islamic faith and society with the vampiric condition - defining how vampires should live, and how their world should intersect with that of humans. They could be the ones using (something that is metaphysically akin to) Carthian Law, though in terms of their role among vampires, they'd be more akin to the Invictus. The relationship between the two could vary quite widely from domain to domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T16:23:57-07:00","id":1110685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109766-islamic-branch-of-the-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1110542#post1110542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said earlier, Islamic mythology includes the potential for nonhuman adherents in a way that Christian mythology doesn't,</div> </div> </div> </div> It does, but that's still forcing them to adhere to something with a human mindset, designed for humans. That's not appropriate for the game as a whole, however. Covenants should be monstrous by nature, to the point that joining one is a breaking point. Real world Islam does not take into account vampire (or djinn, or whatever) psychology and mindsets, and any covenant absolutely should do that. <br /> <br /> Now, if there were bits of the Quran that were hidden from humans meant specifically for vampires by the Seal of the Prophets, and address non-human thoughts, that's cool. That would be awesome, and work great. But a direct transplant of Islam as we understand in in the real world for vampires to follow is unthematic for the game. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, it doesn't have to be just one covenant. </div> </div> </div> I think that there's a very notable difference between having a covenant with belief in a religion, and being an actual priesthood. Take Requiem for Rome. The Camarilla was based entirely on the Greco-Roman gods, and the three main Wings followed them; even still, we had one devoted to being the priesthood. Take some of the settings in Ancient Mysteries/Bloodlines - they're all followers of their culture's religion, but again we tend to see one that dominates as the priesthood, while others are not. Hells, early Lance - Invictus partnerships, before the ascent of Cruac and the Movement from the Gallos Post, included the same mindset.<br /> <br /> I feel like this is the kind of thing you're going with. Personally, I consider it a matter of course, and the core book's division of religions to be a modern aberation rather than something found throughout the game's history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T02:00:22-07:00","id":1140454,"title":"","content":"NOTE: I wrote this for another similar thread, I figured it would make sense to post it here, too. If you see some references to what others have said, it might be from the other thread.<br /> <br /> Hi, everybody,<br /> <br /> I am Muslim and I bumped into this thread as I was planning to narrate a chronicle set in Cordoba in the year 1000 CE, so culturally-Muslim vampires will feature heavily.<br /> <br /> Note: I only became aware of the Banu Shaytan and Iblic Creed stuff reading your posts, and I am going to check them out immediately. Thank you.<br /> <br /> First, to be clear: Islam's abrogations of previous revelations does not mean they stop being true and of divine origin. It simply means that the norms they set are no more binding and that, if they say something explicitly denied by the Quran (such as Jesus - peace be upon him - being the Son of God), that is to be considered a human addition. Beyond this, Muslims throughout history, even pious ones reputed to be saints/walis, have had all sorts of attitudes to previous religions. Also, there are some Muslims who do not believe in abrogation and see previous religions as still valid, though they are few and criticized for this. They exist, nonetheless, so Muslim-cultured Kindred might well claim similar ideas.<br /> <br /> My personal take on the Lancea et Sanctum as seen by vampires in Muslim lands is this: when Islam appeared, the Byzantine Empire was mostly Sanctified (i.e.: LeS), Arabia was Circle of the Crone and Persia (Zoroastrianism) was CotC or something else (still need to figure it out, since Persian stuff does not feature in my Cordoba chronicle).<br /> Early human converts to Islam, once embraced, would not find Muslim guides in their vampirism. The closest thing they would find were Sanctified teachers. Longinism would make more sense to them than adapting Islam to vampirism because:<br /> 1) Islam's religious precepts are evidently not appliable to vampires;<br /> 2) only God can issue religious norms, so vampires can't just take the five pillars, dietary restrictions and other rules and adapt them to vampires (like five prayers at night, don't drink blood of drunkards or pig-eaters, starve to torpor/frenzy in Ramadan, etc), as one would need divine authority for that. Regarding the prayers, I prefer not making them perform any of the five daily prayers, not even the night ones, on the basis that, drinking human blood and being more or less walking corpses, they would be considered ritually impure in various schools of Islamic law, thus being forbidden from performing the five obligatory prayers (although they can perform other forms of prayer that do not require ritual purity, such as dhikr - the remembrance of God - or dua - supplication and personal conversation with God);<br /> 3) Muslims acknowledge previous prophets, including Jesus (peace be upon him), so the tale of Longinus receiving guidance can work. Theologically, he may be classed as a wali (saint) from the community of Jesus, as opposed to a prophet in the strict Islamic theological sense, and this would make things easier;<br /> 4) surah al-Jinn (72nd surah of the Quran) says some Jinn were listening to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) once while he was reciting the Quran and recognised its divine origin. In general, Jinn are believed to be of different kinds, to descend from Iblis/Lucifer/the Devil/Shaytan/Satan, to be responsible for part of polytheism (as jinns made humans worship them as gods), to be able to mate with humans and have offspring from them at times, to have free will, to follow different religions - the same humans follow, since, as far as I learnt, they do not get their own prophets but are guided by human prophets and saints, hence the idea of Longinus being a wali/saint instead of a vampire prophet. Muslim-cultured vampires may see themselves as a sub-species of Jinn (the Strix may well be another sub-species), especially if this is how Arabian pre-Islamic vampires saw themselves. Whichever vampire claimed to have interacted with the Prophet (peace be upon him) or his Companions and received instructions from them may have simply said that the main order was to carry on with Longinism, just knowing that Jesus is not God or His Son, etc., but without prescribed rules that differ from Longinism;<br /> 5) the Quran and the Hadith do not mention (to my knowledge) what rules Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) set for the Jinn, although it's generally understood that they did receive rules from him and previous prophets (peace be upon them all), so whatever rules Longinism imposes on vampires, that can be claimed as the rules set for them;<br /> 6) Longinism does not see Longinus as God, but only as a kind of prophet. This does not overtly contrast the Islamic creed, although it would make it slightly in theological debates easier to see Longinus as a wali/saint or sort of mystical disciple of Jesus. As a wali, he could still receive visions and inspirations, though there are some slight theological differences between walis and prophets.<br /> 7) there are various interpretations of the verses of the Quran about the crucifixion. It's enough to say that Longinian &quot;Muslim&quot; vampires stick to the view that Jesus (peace be upon him) was put on the cross, pierced by Longinus, and then taken up to heaven (before dying). <br /> <br /> In my setting, a Lancea et Sanctum Council was called in Damascus in 800 CE and established that the Church of Longinus was independent of the developments of human religions and its members were free to believe that Muhammad (peace be upon him) was a prophet or not, settling the issue for most adherents (obviously there can always be minor conflicts and divisions here and there, but they don't entail the forming of a wholly different Covenant). Moreover, vampires were not meant to push humans to one or the other Abrahamic religion, as this could effectively harm the appeal of that religion, but only remind humans of God, making them fear Him, tempt them to test them, and fight the Circle of the Crone and any vampire who promoted polytheism or atheism.<br /> <br /> I assume that there are vampires who carry on their mortal religion (whether Islam or Christianity or Judaism or other), but these usually act alone and have not formed proper Covenants that can rival with the LeS. It is quite common for new vampires, too, to hang onto one's mortal religion for a while, but this is usually temporary. One exception that I plan to include in the Chronicle is a group of vampire vampire-hunters called &quot;at-Tawwabun&quot; (the Repentant), who believe the only way to be forgiven by God is by killing other vampires and feeding only from animals forbidden to Muslims (ex.: pigs and predatory animals). This would be an antagonist covenant, however, not open to players. I have more interesting ideas about them, but I'll share them in time, God willing.<br /> <br /> In my Cordoba, the Bishop/Great Imam of the Lancea et Sanctum/ar-Rumh wal-Quds (I use double names to reflect the double culture of the vampires of Muslim Spain) has imposed on the city's vampire to feed only from sinful humans and not to kill the kine, unless they were condemned to death by the human authorities. In addition to this, Longinians are encouraged to shepherd the flock they belonged to in life (vampires who were Muslim prey on Muslims and vampires who were Christian prey on Christians), as they are most likely to understand how to remind their victims of God, but this is only an encouragement.<br /> <br /> I hope all the above makes sense. I am going to read the material about the Banu Shaytan and see how that is, God willing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}